Spin(3) (B1): C_2(vector) = 2, C_2(spinor) = 3/4, n(n-1)/8 = 3/4
Spin(4) (D2): C_2(vector) = 3, C_2(spinor) = 3/2, n(n-1)/8 = 3/2
Spin(5) (B2): C_2(vector) = 4, C_2(spinor) = 5/2, n(n-1)/8 = 5/2
Spin(6) (D3): C_2(vector) = 5, C_2(spinor) = 15/4, n(n-1)/8 = 15/4
Spin(7) (B3): C_2(vector) = 6, C_2(spinor) = 21/4, n(n-1)/8 = 21/4
Spin(8) (D4): C_2(vector) = 7, C_2(spinor) = 7, n(n-1)/8 = 7
Spin(2) = U(1): the spinor charge 1/2 has C_2 = (1/2)^2 = 1/4 = 2*1/8
